NAME
       paste - join the lines of files side by side

SYNOPSIS
       paste [-d DELIMITERS] [-s] FILE...

DESCRIPTION
       paste writes line 1 of every file on one output line, separated by
       tabs, then line 2 of every file, and so on. With -s it joins all the
       lines of each file into one line instead. A FILE named - is standard
       input.

OPTIONS
       -d, --delimiters LIST
              Use these characters instead of tabs (used in turn).

       -s, --serial
              Join all lines of one file onto one line.

EXAMPLES
       Two columns side by side, separated by commas:

           paste -d, names.txt phones.txt

       All user names on one line, separated by spaces:

           cut -d: -f1 /etc/passwd | paste -s -d' '

SEE ALSO
       cut(1), join(1), column(1)
